{
  "id": "u02-l02",
  "unit": "u02-pronouns",
  "title": "We & they",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Add **-রা** (*-ra*) to make pronouns plural:\n\n- আমি → **আমরা** (*amra*) we\n- তুমি → **তোমরা** (*tomra*), আপনি → **আপনারা** (*apnara*) you all\n- সে → **তারা** (*tara*), ও → **ওরা** (*ora*) they (ওরা is the everyday spoken form)\n\n**The verb does not change for plural**: আমি ভালো **আছি**, আমরা ভালো **আছি**; আপনি **আছেন**, আপনারা **আছেন**. The ending only cares about *person* and *respect*.\n\nNouns usually need no plural ending: **তারা ডাক্তার** = 'They are doctors.' **ছেলে / মেয়ে** mean 'boy / girl' and also 'son / daughter'.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "amra",
      "bn": "আমরা",
      "tr": "amra",
      "en": "we"
    },
    {
      "id": "tomra",
      "bn": "তোমরা",
      "tr": "tomra",
      "en": "you (familiar, plural)"
    },
    {
      "id": "apnara",
      "bn": "আপনারা",
      "tr": "apnara",
      "en": "you (polite, plural)"
    },
    {
      "id": "tara",
      "bn": "তারা",
      "tr": "tara",
      "en": "they",
      "notes": "Plural of সে. Polite plural: ওনারা (onara) / তাঁরা."
    },
    {
      "id": "ora",
      "bn": "ওরা",
      "tr": "ora",
      "en": "they (spoken)",
      "notes": "Plural of ও; the everyday spoken 'they'."
    },
    {
      "id": "chhele",
      "bn": "ছেলে",
      "tr": "chhele",
      "en": "boy",
      "notes": "Also 'son' (আমার ছেলে = my son), and loosely 'young man'."
    },
    {
      "id": "meye",
